# ---- build output -------------------------------------------------------
# The binary, with or without a Windows .exe suffix, and stray build leftovers.
# Matching both names matters: Go appends .exe on Windows, and a stale `dirserve`
# from a Linux/WSL build can sit next to it.
/dirserve
/dirserve.exe
*.exe
*.exe~
*~

# ---- coverage / test output ---------------------------------------------
*.out
*.test
coverage.*

# ---- local data served by the container ----------------------------------
# The compose stack mounts a host directory here; it is user data, never source.
/data
/data/

# ---- editor / OS noise --------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- local overrides ----------------------------------------------------
# Real .env files hold the serve token; the committed example does not.
.env
.env.local
docker-compose.override.yml

# Local build spec, not part of the published project
/DIRSERVE.md
